# Project guidance

Purpose: maintain an independent Python project using the **{{ profile }}** profile.

Prepare with `python scripts/project.py bootstrap`; check with `python scripts/project.py check`; build and check with `python scripts/project.py verify`.
Use `python scripts/project.py context --next` for the next READY item, `python scripts/project.py status` for read-only health, `python scripts/project.py sync` for generated indexes/map, and `python scripts/project.py package-check` for offline installed-wheel smoke.

Search before reading: find the relevant symbol, path, and neighboring tests first; open only those files and expand context when evidence requires it.

Follow [docs/agent/index.md](docs/agent/index.md) for work-type routing and [the context-efficiency standard](docs/agent/standards/context-efficiency.md) for context selection.

{% if profile == "minimal" -%}
Architecture invariants: keep the `src/` layout direct and do not add layers until a concrete requirement needs them. Keep dependencies minimal and do not add a runtime dependency on AgentReady.
{% elif profile == "application" -%}
Architecture invariants: place capabilities under `modules/<capability>/`; keep entrypoints thin and composition in bootstrap; domain stays independent of outer layers. Keep dependencies minimal and do not add a runtime dependency on AgentReady.
{% else -%}
Architecture invariants: place capabilities under `modules/<capability>/`; keep entrypoints thin, adapters dependent inward, and composition in bootstrap. Keep dependencies minimal and do not add a runtime dependency on AgentReady.
{% endif -%}

Minimum coherent diff: make the smallest change that satisfies the acceptance criteria and avoid speculative directories, abstractions, or refactors.

For implementation work, select one READY item, use its Type to choose the workflow in `docs/agent/index.md`, read its normative specification and only relevant standards, preserve requirements, update the implementation record and documentation impact, then sync the registry and changelog. If blocked, record why, mark BLOCKED, and stop.
Human-owned work items live in `docs/work/`.
